          "filename": "Hitchcock-steps-1.jpg",
          "caption": "View down the \"Exorcist steps,\" also known as the \"Hitchcock Steps,\" a steep staircase connecting Prospect and M Streets in Georgetown, DC.  The site's role in movie history and its challenging grade make it a popular destination for both curiosity-seekers and Georgetown University fitness enthusiasts. It can be seen in \"The Exorcist\" film, and was featured prominently in the 1971 novel by author William Peter Blatty, who reportedly lived in Georgetown in the 1960's.",
